            <formatted-text>
              <run bold='true'>Note on the handling of treatment:</run>
              <run>&#10;Treatment is a property of a </run>
              <run bold='true'>vendor. </run>
              <run>Single fee events are attached to one specific vendor and therefore have only one possible treatment value, but multiple fee events (such as creating a session or loading the listing page) are considered </run>
              <run bold='true'>both</run>
              <run> treatment = true </run>
              <run bold='true'>and</run>
              <run> treatment = false.&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true'>Note on the handling of target group:</run>
              <run>
Target group is also a property of a </run>
              <run bold='true'>vendor</run>
              <run>. Only sessions that reached the menu page (or a later single fee event) can have a target group value. For this reason, CVR, mCVR2 and User CVR are not available when filtering for target group. CVR3 (# transaction / # menu page) should be used instead.</run>
